ALGORITHM: Trapping Rain Water

1. Start.

2. Initialize:
       left = 0
       right = length of height - 1
       left_max = 0
       right_max = 0
       water = 0

3. Repeat while left < right:

       If height[left] < height[right]:

           If height[left] >= left_max:
               left_max = height[left]

           Else:
               water = water + left_max - height[left]

           Move left one position forward.

       Otherwise:

           If height[right] >= right_max:
               right_max = height[right]

           Else:
               water = water + right_max - height[right]

           Move right one position backward.

4. Return water.

TIME COMPLEXITY:
O(n)

SPACE COMPLEXITY:
O(1)
